# Translations TODO

This file documents all hardcoded strings and missing translations found in the codebase.
These should be translated and added to all locale files later.

## Core File System (js/core.fs.js)

### Error Messages
- `"Not a directory: " + path` (line 79)
  - Should use: `fs.notADirectory` or similar
  - Context: When trying to list a non-directory path

- `"Parent is not a directory"` (lines 85, 102, 124)
  - Should use: `fs.parentNotADirectory` or similar
  - Context: When parent path is not a directory

- `"A folder named \"${name}\" already exists in this location"` (line 90)
  - Should use: `files.folderAlreadyExists` (already exists but FS throws this)
  - Context: When creating a folder that already exists

- `"Parent directory not found"` (line 152)
  - Should use: `fs.parentDirectoryNotFound` or similar
  - Context: When parent directory doesn't exist

- `"File not found: " + path` (lines 154, 157)
  - Should use: `terminal.fileNotFound` (already exists)
  - Context: When file doesn't exist

- `"Not a file: " + path` (line 159)
  - Should use: `terminal.notAFile` (already exists)
  - Context: When path is not a file

- `"Parent directory not found or not a directory"` (line 193)
  - Should use: `fs.parentDirectoryNotFoundOrNotDirectory` or similar
  - Context: When parent doesn't exist or isn't a directory

- `"Path not found or type mismatch"` (line 198)
  - Should use: `fs.pathNotFoundOrTypeMismatch` or similar
  - Context: When path doesn't exist or type doesn't match

- `"Path not found"` (line 206)
  - Should use: `terminal.pathNotFound` (already exists)
  - Context: When path doesn't exist

- `"A ${itemType} named \"${newName}\" already exists in this location."` (line 222)
  - Should use: `files.nameAlreadyExists` (already exists but FS throws this)
  - Context: When renaming to a name that already exists

### Storage Quota Error
- `"Storage quota exceeded. File system is ${sizeMB} MB (${sizeKB} KB) with ${fileCount} files. Please delete some files to free up space."` (line 35)
  - Should use: `fs.storageQuotaExceeded` with placeholders
  - Context: When localStorage quota is exceeded
  - Placeholders: {sizeMB}, {sizeKB}, {fileCount}

## Terminal App (js/apps/terminal.js)

### Fallback Messages (when I18n.t() returns undefined)
- `"Both a file and folder named \"${targetName}\" exist. Please specify type: use \"rm file ${targetName}\" for file or \"rm dir ${targetName}\" for folder."` (line 474)
  - Key: `terminal.ambiguousPathRm` (already exists, but fallback is hardcoded)
  - Context: When both file and folder exist for rm command

- `"Both a file and folder named \"${srcName}\" exist. Please specify type: use \"cp file ${srcName} ${destName}\" for file or \"cp dir ${srcName} ${destName}\" for folder."` (line 523)
  - Key: `terminal.ambiguousPath` (already exists, but fallback is hardcoded)
  - Context: When both file and folder exist for cp command

- `"Both a file and folder named \"${srcName}\" exist. Please specify type: use \"mv file ${srcName} ${destName}\" for file or \"mv dir ${srcName} ${destName}\" for folder."` (line 620)
  - Key: `terminal.ambiguousPath` (already exists, but fallback is hardcoded)
  - Context: When both file and folder exist for mv command

### Hardcoded Text
- `"destination"` (lines 521, 618)
  - Should use: `terminal.destination` or similar
  - Context: Default destination name in error messages

- `"🟦"` (line 699)
  - This is an emoji fallback, probably fine to keep as-is
  - Context: Default app icon when none is provided

